  "name": "Question 8",
  "problem": "Consider the set $B,$ defined as\n\n$$\nB={3{n}^{2}-2:n\\in {-1,0,1,2,3}}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following sets is equivalent to $B?$",
  "worked_solution": "The elements of $B$ are all the terms of the sequence ${b}_{n},$ given by\n\n$$\n{b}_{n}=3{n}^{2}-2,\\,n\\in {-1,0,1,2,3}.\n$$\n\nLet's write down all the terms of our sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{-1} & =3(-1)^{2}-2=3-2=1 \\\\ {b}_{0} & =3(0)^{2}-2=0-2=-2 \\\\ {b}_{1} & =3(1)^{2}-2=3-2=1 \\\\ {b}_{2} & =3(2)^{2}-2=12-2=10 \\\\ {b}_{3} & =3(3)^{2}-2=27-2=25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nB={1,-2,1,10,25}={1,-2,10,25}.\n$$",
